Phasmid: Web Bluetooth and Web Share as on Windows

What:     A Windows profile gets navigator.bluetooth and navigator.share and
          canShare, as Windows Chrome has them. getAvailability() reports
          capabilities.bluetooth_available, never the host's BlueZ;
          requestDevice() without a claimed adapter rejects as on Windows
          without one. share() runs the stock checks and then ends as a
          dismissed share sheet: AbortError. Linux profiles are unchanged.
Why:      Windows Chrome always exposes both APIs and Linux Chrome neither,
          so their absence names Linux. Without a ShareService binder a
          share() call would kill the renderer.
Profile:  capabilities.bluetooth, capabilities.web_share,
          capabilities.bluetooth_available
Hooks:    chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
          SetRuntimeFeaturesDefaultsBeforeBlinkInitialization;
          chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
          PopulateChromeFrameBinders;
          chrome/browser/webshare/share_service_impl.cc RunShareOperation;
          content/browser/bluetooth/web_bluetooth_service_impl.cc
          WebBluetoothServiceImpl::GetAvailability;
          content/browser/bluetooth/bluetooth_device_chooser_controller.cc
          BluetoothDeviceChooserController::GetDevice; BUILD.gn files
Contexts: main, iframe; both APIs are window-only, as in stock
Guard:    tests/guards/platform/bluetooth-share.py

